{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "Item chance-on-hit procs use the ppm rate their tooltip states",
  "contract": [
    "Chance-on-hit item spells whose tooltip states '(N ppm)' were stored with spellppmRate 0. The core then ignores the stated rate: a spell with ProcChance 100 fires on every damaging hit and one with ProcChance 101 falls back to weapon delay * 1.8 percent. The data fix copies each spell's stated ppm into spellppmRate.",
    "Sludge Hammer 1379518 (delay 2600) carries spell 313142 with ProcChance 100 and tooltip 1ppm. Over 300 seconds of 2.6 s swings about 115 hits land, so 1ppm (4.3 percent per hit) gives about 5 procs, while a proc on every hit gives about 115.",
    "Ghost Buster 5ppm and Cursed Ritual Carver 3ppm (ProcChance 101), Searsteel Claymore 0.7ppm (ProcChance 100) and the three Carapace Cracker tiers 2.2/2.4/2.6ppm are asserted from the stored rate, which was 0 before the fix. Glaive of the Pit 28774 keeps its existing 1.6 rate."
  ],
  "timeout_ms": 420000,
